0,"Holes and","channels"]],"src":"t"},"specks":{"doing":"Specks school in open water over the deepest flats, channels and offshore grass, suspended at a different depth from day to day.","how":[["Drift or troll","Missouri minnows or grass shrimp, or spider-rig small jigs (hair jigs, tubes, Hal Flies)."],["Find the depth","Set minnows at several depths, then match the one that bites."],["Sonar","Cast a small jig to schools you see on forward-facing sonar."]],"bands":[[3,10,"Open-water","schools"]],"src":"t"},"bream":{"doing":"Slow. Bluegill and shellcracker hold in deeper grass, canals and around docks; warm, sunny afternoons bring them up.","how":[["Deep grass","Grass shrimp on the bottom next to hydrilla or eelgrass."],["Canals","Small jig or worm along canal edges and docks."]],"bands":[[4,8,"Deep grass","and canals"]],"src":"t"}},"prespawn":{"flbass":{"doing":"Fall and early winter bring good-sized pre-spawn bass. They feed along the outer edge of the emergent grass, often on eelgrass, ahead of the spawn.","how":[["Topwater","Buzzbaits and prop baits as the pre-spawn starts."],["Live bait","Golden shiners are the best live bait for big Florida bass."],["Where","Eelgrass along the outside edge of the reeds and cattails."]],"bands":[[1,4,"Reeds and","maidencane"],[4,8,"Outside","grass edge"]],"src":"r"},"specks":{"doing":"Schools leave the open water for pad fields, bulrush and Kissimmee grass that sit next to deeper water. A cold front pushes them back out.","how":[["Edges","Troll or drift minnow-tipped jigs along the outside of the pads and reeds."],["Holes","Minnow under a cork in openings at the grass edge."],["After a front","Fish the closest open water off the same grass."]],"bands":[[2,7,"Grass edges","by deep water"]],"src":"t"},"bream":{"doing":"Shellcracker move onto firm sand and shell near the grass ahead of the spring full moons; bluegill feed around reeds and docks.","how":[["Shellcracker","Red wigglers on the bottom with a split shot."],["Bluegill","Crickets or grass shrimp under a small float along reeds."]],"bands":[[2,6,"Sand flats","near grass"]],"src":"t"}},"spawn":{"flbass":{"doing":"Peak spawn is late winter into early spring. Water level is everything: a small rise spreads bass across wide areas and into sawgrass and reeds.","how":[["South Bay","Look for holes in the wiregrass \"hay\"; a white creature bait or wacky-rigged Senko for bedding fish."],["The Shoal","Flip the pencil reeds with a jig; shad schools and diving gulls mean feeding bass."],["Bottom baits","Black and blue creature bait into holes, with longer soak times once fish settle on beds."],["Moving","White or watermelon-red swim jig when fish are cruising."]],"bands":[[1,4,"Beds on sand","in the grass"]],"src":"r"},"specks":{"doing":"January is usually the best month for keeper specks. Fish the edges of the vegetation early and late in the day.","how":[["Edges","Minnow-tipped jig or a minnow under a float along the grass."],["Sonar","Cast small jigs to fish on forward-facing sonar, or spider-rig."]],"bands":[[1,4,"Pads and","reeds"]],"src":"r"},"bream":{"doing":"Shellcracker bed on the March and April full moons on firm sand and shell near grass. Bluegill start as the water warms.","how":[["Beds","Red wigglers on the bottom; work the area until you find the colony."],["Spinners","Small beetle spin along the edge of the flat."]],"bands":[[2,5,"Shellcracker","beds"]],"src":"t"}},"latespring":{"flbass":{"doing":"Post-spawn bass slide to sparse pads and submerged hydrilla. Topwater at first light, then moving baits over the grass.","how":[["Dawn","Popping frog or prop bait over sparse pads."],["Later","Swim jig or vibrating jig over submerged hydrilla."]],"bands":[[0,3,"Topwater","at dawn"],[3,8,"Grass lines","first drop"]],"src":"r"},"specks":{"doing":"After the spawn, specks scatter to deeper grass edges, docks, bridges and channel edges. The bite slows as the water warms.","how":[["Structure","Minnows at dock pilings, bridges and fish attractors."],["Grass lines","Small jig swum along the deep edge of the vegetation."]],"bands":[[3,9,"Docks, bridges,","grass edges"]],"src":"t"},"bream":{"doing":"Bluegill bed in colonies on sand around each full moon from April on: the best bream fishing of the year, with fish near a pound on good lakes.","how":[["Crickets","Under a cork over the beds or along reed lines."],["Grass shrimp","In deep spatterdock and grass patches."],["Fly rod","Popping bug or small spider at dawn and dusk."]],"bands":[[1,4,"Bluegill","beds"]],"src":"t"}},"summer":{"flbass":{"doing":"Low water from June to August pulls fish to the outside edges. Bass hide under hyacinth, hydrilla and pennywort mats; Moonshine Bay holds them all year.","how":[["Punch","1 to 1.5 oz tungsten, 65 lb braid and a stout flipping rod."],["Early","Moving baits along the outside edges."],["Worms","Texas-rigged grape or black worms; frogs over the mats."]],"bands":[[0,3,"Topwater","early"],[1,5,"Under","the mats"],[6,10,"Offshore grass","and shell"]],"src":"r"},"specks":{"doing":"The slowest season. Specks suspend in the deepest water, on fish attractors and in shade; fish early, late or at night.","how":[["Night","Lights and minnows at bridges and deep docks."],["Attractors","Vertical jig or minnow at the depth you mark."]],"bands":[[5,12,"Deepest water","and attractors"]],"src":"t"},"bream":{"doing":"Bluegill and shellcracker fish very well in summer, and are still in the marsh as summer ends.","how":[["Bluegill","Grass shrimp, red worms, crickets or beetle spins."],["Shellcracker","Live worms on the bottom."]],"bands":[[1,4,"Beds on","the full moon"],[4,8,"Deep pads","and docks"]],"src":"r"}},"fall":{"flbass":{"doing":"Bass school after shad and shiners as the water cools, and the pre-spawn bite starts building.","how":[["Schools","Lipless crankbait, spinnerbait or swimbait at wind-blown reed points and open hydrilla clumps."],["Settled fish","Switch to soft plastics once the school settles."],["Shiners","Wild shiners as the big fish start to feed."]],"bands":[[0,4,"Schooling","on shad"],[3,8,"Grass edges"]],"src":"r"},"specks":{"doing":"Specks slow down in summer and pick up in November and December. The south end has been the best area lately.","how":[["Find them","Suspend minnows at several depths; use sonar and keep moving until you find a school."],["Jig","Jigging is the most efficient way once you find them."],["Limit","Release specks under 10 inches; 25 a day."]],"bands":[[3,10,"Open-water","schools"]],"src":"r"},"bream":{"doing":"Bream feed hard in the grass as the water cools. Fewer beds, steady numbers.","how":[["Grass","Anchor near a thick hydrilla patch and fish grass shrimp or worms near the bottom."],["Reeds","Crickets under a cork along reed lines."]],"bands":[[2,6,"Grass","patches"]],"src":"t"}}},"zones":[{"sp":"flbass","p":["prespawn","spawn"],"name":"South Bay","t":"Wiregrass \"hayfields\", reeds and pads over hard bottom.","src":"r","c":[[739,1153,50],[713,1122,40],[620,1120,45]]},{"sp":"flbass","p":["spawn","latespring"],"name":"Observation Shoal","t":"Pencil reeds halfway up the west side; shad and diving gulls.","src":"r","c":[[315,820,45],[314,808,35],[311,789,35]]},{"sp":"flbass","p":["spawn","summer"],"name":"Moonshine and Fisheating bays","t":"West-side pads, hydrilla and eelgrass; the Monkey Box area here is a spawning magnet in high water.","src":"r","c":[[177,734,45],[30,539,45],[90,600,40]]},{"sp":"flbass","p":["prespawn","latespring","summer"],"name":"Harney Pond and Indian Prairie","t":"Matted hydrilla and hyacinth; protected when it blows.","src":"r","c":[[73,515,50],[305,390,45]]},{"sp":"flbass","p":["prespawn","spawn","fall"],"name":"North Shore cattails","t":"Miles of cattails behind a big hydrilla flat, out of the north wind.","src":"r","c":[[680,60,50],[790,120,45],[600,110,40]]},{"sp":"flbass","p":["summer","fall"],"name":"Kissimmee River mouth","t":"Current seams and isolated grass where the river comes in.","src":"r","c":[[565,45,40]]},{"sp":"flbass","p":["latespring"],"name":"East-side hydrilla flats","t":"Grass flats near the fish camps; topwater frogs on calm mornings.","src":"r","c":[[777,107,45],[841,265,40]]},{"sp":"specks","p":["prespawn","spawn","fall"],"name":"South end","t":"Open water and grass edges; the best speck area lately.","src":"r","c":[[410,1005,45],[550,1060,50],[804,1007,40]]},{"sp":"specks","p":["fall","prespawn"],"name":"Kissimmee River and canals","t":"Minnow-tipped jigs and spider rigs.","src":"r","c":[[565,45,40],[792,728,35]]},{"sp":"specks","p":["spawn"],"name":"West-side grass edges","t":"Pads and Kissimmee grass by deeper water.","src":"t","c":[[315,820,40],[177,734,40]]},{"sp":"specks","p":["latespring","summer"],"name":"Deep edges and canals","t":"Shade and the deepest water; early, late or under lights.","src":"t","c":[[792,728,35],[410,1005,40]]},{"sp":"bream","p":["latespring","summer","fall"],"name":"Marsh edges","t":"Bluegill and shellcracker in the marsh and grass.","src":"r","c":[[177,734,40],[30,539,40],[739,1153,40]]},{"sp":"bream","p":["prespawn","spawn","latespring"],"name":"North Shore sand","t":"Shellcracker beds near the cattails.","src":"t","c":[[680,60,40]]}],"sources":[["FWC: Lake Okeechobee","https://myfwc.com/fishing/freshwater/sites-forecasts/s/lake-okeechobee/"],["Major League Fishing: 5 key areas on Okeechobee","https://majorleaguefishing.com/news/2016-02-03-5-key-areas-on-okeechobee"],["Bassmaster: Hot spots, Lake Okeechobee","https://develop.bassmaster.com/hot-spots/news/hot-spots-lake-okeechobee/"],["FishUSA: Lake Okeechobee bass fishing","https://www.fishusa.com/learn/lake-okeechobee-bass-fishing/"],["Florida Sportsman: crappie hotspots","https://www.floridasportsman.com/editorial/crappie-hotspots-florida/542513"]]}